WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.240
Movie the long flight of courage. Have you ever wondered how migratory birds know where to go when seasons change?

00:08.740 --> 00:14.820
Migration is a fascinating natural phenomenon. It's a cyclical journey that many bird species embark on

00:15.420 --> 00:19.780
Traveling thousands of miles between their breeding and wintering grounds, but why do they migrate?

00:20.620 --> 00:22.820
The answer is simple to survive

00:23.420 --> 00:28.100
Birds migrate to areas where food is more abundant and the climate is more favorable

00:28.200 --> 00:33.580
This movement is governed by the changing of the seasons. Now, let's delve into the real mystery

00:33.620 --> 00:35.800
How do these birds know where to go?

00:35.940 --> 00:40.600
How do they navigate such vast distances often in the dark without getting lost?

00:40.960 --> 00:45.140
The answer lies in the Earth's magnetic field and visual landmarks

00:45.660 --> 00:49.620
Birds have a remarkable ability to sense the Earth's magnetic field

00:49.940 --> 00:55.300
This geomagnetic sense acts as a natural compass guiding them on their long journeys

00:55.580 --> 01:00.360
It's like they have a built-in GPS system that keeps them on track, but that's not all

01:00.740 --> 01:03.620
Birds also use visual landmarks to navigate

01:03.780 --> 01:10.520
They recognize coastlines, mountain ranges and rivers which serve as natural signposts on their migratory route

01:10.700 --> 01:15.220
But the journey is far from easy. These flights demand incredible physical endurance

01:15.820 --> 01:18.540
Birds must prepare themselves for this grueling journey

01:18.780 --> 01:21.540
They bulk up storing fat to use as fuel

01:21.720 --> 01:27.780
Some species can double or even triple their body weight in preparation for migration and once they take off

01:27.780 --> 01:31.400
They must maintain a high level of stamina to complete their journey

01:32.100 --> 01:34.720
Imagine running a marathon, but not for a few hours

01:35.460 --> 01:41.780
Instead for days or even weeks without any rest. That's the kind of physical feat these birds pull off

01:41.940 --> 01:43.940
It's truly awe-inspiring

01:44.220 --> 01:51.060
In essence, migration is a test of survival. It's a long arduous journey that birds must undertake twice a year

01:51.380 --> 01:57.380
They navigate using the Earth's magnetic field and visual landmarks and prepare their bodies for extreme endurance

01:57.820 --> 02:01.860
It's a journey that requires endurance, precision and a keen sense of direction

02:02.700 --> 02:08.740
Imagine flying thousands of miles without a map or GPS guided only by your instincts and the stars above

02:09.020 --> 02:11.540
This is the reality for migratory birds

02:11.860 --> 02:19.020
Each year these winged adventurers embark on an odyssey that takes them across continents oceans and vast unending skies

02:20.140 --> 02:25.140
Their journey begins at the cusp of the seasons a time when the earth is changing its attire and

02:25.540 --> 02:28.300
Survival in their home terrain becomes an uphill battle

02:28.980 --> 02:36.020
With an innate sense as old as their species they take to the skies leaving behind the familiar for the unknown

02:36.860 --> 02:42.460
Imagine the strength of their wings beating tirelessly against the wind the Sun the rain

02:43.260 --> 02:48.180
imagine the courage in their tiny hearts facing predators waiting in the shadows and

02:48.380 --> 02:52.780
The tempestuous weather that can turn from friend to foe in a heartbeat

02:53.740 --> 02:56.900
Consider the human-made obstacles they encounter along the way

02:57.540 --> 03:03.460
bright city lights that disorient them tall structures that stand as imposing barriers and

03:03.940 --> 03:10.180
Noisy machines that drown out their communication calls and yet they navigate through it all

03:10.860 --> 03:14.600
Demonstrating a resilience. That's nothing short of awe inspiring

03:15.300 --> 03:18.060
But the journey is not all hardship

03:18.220 --> 03:25.700
There are stopover sites little havens scattered across their flight path where they can rest refuel and rejuvenate

03:26.420 --> 03:33.100
These sites are crucial providing a brief respite from the relentless flight here. They replenish their energy

03:33.740 --> 03:37.700
Feeding on the abundant resources before taking to the skies once more

03:38.300 --> 03:44.700
Their journey fraught with danger and uncertainty is a testament to their resilience and a marvel of nature

03:45.500 --> 03:50.820
The next time you see a flock of birds flying overhead remember they're on a journey of survival

03:51.340 --> 03:56.540
Guided by instincts honed over millions of years and as they disappear into the horizon

03:57.180 --> 04:01.220
Spare a thought for their incredible journey for it is a story of courage

04:01.220 --> 04:04.420
Determination and the indomitable spirit of life itself

